1
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:06,284
No, no, no, no... oh, come on!

2
00:00:06,419 --> 00:00:08,917
Oh, man! That was so close.

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:11,428
Theo. Buddy.

4
00:00:11,673 --> 00:00:13,626
You are such a screwup.

5
00:00:14,751 --> 00:00:17,003
Yeah. I know.

6
00:00:20,493 --> 00:00:22,775
Here's the thing about a joke.

7
00:00:23,185 --> 00:00:28,101
It only works... when everyone in the room knows it isn't true.

8
00:00:28,841 --> 00:00:31,449
Theo didn't say it like a joke.

9
00:00:32,409 --> 00:00:39,489
And with three people in the room, that kind of silence doesn't just get heavy. It multiplies.

10
00:00:40,229 --> 00:00:42,699
I think I'll... head home.

11
00:00:42,999 --> 00:00:44,785
Text me, okay?

12
00:00:50,255 --> 00:00:53,041
Come on, man. I was kidding.

13
00:00:53,176 --> 00:00:54,977
You know I was kidding.

14
00:00:55,827 --> 00:00:57,141
I know you were.

15
00:00:58,101 --> 00:00:59,966
That's kind of the problem.

16
00:01:00,816 --> 00:01:02,808
What's that supposed to mean?

17
00:01:03,768 --> 00:01:09,991
It's never one big thing. It's “relax, sensitive boy.” It's “nice one, genius.”

18
00:01:10,511 --> 00:01:14,887
Every one of them is tiny. Like... two percent.

19
00:01:15,517 --> 00:01:19,613
But I've been collecting two percents for about six months.

20
00:01:20,573 --> 00:01:25,550
So what? Now I have to walk on eggshells in my own apartment?

21
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:29,629
No. I'm not asking you to be careful.

22
00:01:30,259 --> 00:01:32,403
I'm asking you to be curious.

23
00:01:33,803 --> 00:01:37,271
Can I ask you something? And tell me if I'm wrong.

24
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:41,787
When you roast me... what are you actually trying to say?

25
00:01:43,957 --> 00:01:48,471
Anger is often a guard... standing in front of a door.

26
00:01:48,881 --> 00:01:53,087
And behind that door, there's usually something softer.

27
00:01:54,267 --> 00:01:59,154
In my unit... nobody said nice stuff. Ever.

28
00:01:59,894 --> 00:02:06,056
You said, “you're an idiot, get in the truck.” And that meant... I've got you.

29
00:02:07,236 --> 00:02:12,753
There was this guy. Danny. We gave him hell. All of us.

30
00:02:13,273 --> 00:02:17,155
And one day, he just... started agreeing with it.

31
00:02:17,895 --> 00:02:21,707
“Yeah, I'm useless.” “Yeah, I know.”

32
00:02:22,447 --> 00:02:27,378
And we laughed. Took us way too long to figure out he meant it.

33
00:02:28,558 --> 00:02:30,128
Is he okay?

34
00:02:31,088 --> 00:02:32,436
He is now.

35
00:02:33,066 --> 00:02:35,102
No thanks to me.

36
00:02:36,722 --> 00:02:38,701
So when I said it tonight...

37
00:02:39,331 --> 00:02:41,930
Yeah, it scared the crap out of me.

38
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:48,426
So... “you're a screwup” actually means... “you're my guy”?

39
00:02:49,166 --> 00:02:50,447
Basically.

40
00:02:51,187 --> 00:02:56,513
Man. That is the most confusing love language I've ever heard.

41
00:02:58,023 --> 00:03:04,718
I get it now. I do. But I wasn't in your unit. I don't have the translation guide.

42
00:03:05,128 --> 00:03:11,384
When it's just the joke, without the “I've got you” part... the joke is all I hear.

43
00:03:12,454 --> 00:03:17,030
So what am I supposed to do? Look you in the eye and go,

44
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:21,748
“Theo, I value you... as a person”?

45
00:03:23,038 --> 00:03:25,009
Please never do that again.

46
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:34,472
Keep the roasting. Some of it's funny. Just... every once in a while, say the other part out loud.

47
00:03:34,882 --> 00:03:41,879
And if one lands wrong, I'll tell you. Right then. Not six months later. That part's on me.

48
00:03:42,729 --> 00:03:43,765
Deal.

49
00:03:45,715 --> 00:03:49,609
And for the record... you're not a screwup.

50
00:03:50,899 --> 00:03:51,978
I know.

51
00:03:53,488 --> 00:03:57,554
Same two words. A completely different meaning.

52
00:04:03,244 --> 00:04:04,398
Theo.

53
00:04:04,918 --> 00:04:08,857
That is the worst toast I have ever seen in my life.

54
00:04:10,037 --> 00:04:12,461
I'd still go to war with you, though.

55
00:04:12,981 --> 00:04:17,267
That's weirdly the nicest thing anyone's ever said to me.

56
00:04:18,997 --> 00:04:25,998
Most of us were never taught to say the soft thing out loud. So we hide it inside jokes.

57
00:04:26,408 --> 00:04:29,059
The goal isn't to stop joking.

58
00:04:29,359 --> 00:04:34,623
It's to make sure the people we love... can still find the love inside it.

59
00:04:35,253 --> 00:04:39,549
And when they can't... to be brave enough to say so.

